      "problem": "If $y=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We first rewrite the function as\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}=-2{x}^{-4}.\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the constant multiple and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{-4}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-4}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-4){x}^{-5} \\\\  & =8{x}^{-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
